From 35dc6695ebc81974629bf39dafde38b631d2c741 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:16:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(bridge): report how every teleport ends, with its id

A plugin that queued a teleport never learned whether the player moved.
The port of EssentialsX needs that for every teleport command: it keeps
the place before a move that worked for /back, sends its message of
success and charges only then. The teleport also took its place as it
was, so a far home or warp whose chunks no player keeps loaded found no
safe place, since the question safeLocation reads loaded chunks alone.

Every teleport now carries an id that golem-bridge hands out once per
process, and the mod reports its end once with the natives teleported,
with where the player was and is, or teleportFailed, with one reason of
a closed set. A teleport may carry the radius of a search for a safe
place, which the mod runs inside the action: it has the chunks of the
search loaded by a ticket of its own, keyed by the id, over as many
ticks as the game takes, so no tick waits for a chunk, and searches
once they are. The teleports of one player keep their order, a player
who leaves ends theirs before Golem hears it, and the stop ends those
that still wait.

The action teleport gains the id and the radius, the host class two
natives, Event two variants with TeleportFailure, and the context of a
plugin queue_teleport beside teleport. Notebook 04 holds the wire form,
the ids and the reports to the contract, and notebook 05 runs every
outcome but a cancel by a mod and a timeout on a stock Forge.

